--
N5008 [temp.mem.class]/1, [class.nest]/3: a member class of a class template
may be defined outside the class template by a qualified name, here from
outside its namespace (`template <class C> struct ns::S<C>::N { ... };').
The front end grafted an out-of-class member class definition into the
class template only for the form `S<C>::N'; the namespace-qualified form was
ignored and S<char>::N stayed incomplete (bin53).  The graft now accepts a
namespace prefix.  test_nested_namespaces.desc: two namespace levels, also
for an out-of-class member function `a::b::S<C>::f', whose definition was
lost (typecheck_class_template_member, "no body for callee"), and a
specialization instantiated before the member class definition.  g++ 13
and clang++ 18 accept this program, and it fails only its WRONG assertion.
